<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/undated">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">French Revolutionary Wars</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The French Revolutionary Wars (1792–1802) were fought between revolutionary <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and coalitions of European powers. French victories led to the loss of German lands west of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> and the reorganisation of the empire's territories, setting in motion the dissolution of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a> in 1806.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/french-revolutionary-wars.jpg" alt="French Revolutionary Wars" width="187" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ruedi33a · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:French_Revolutionary_Wars.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
